      "Request strike-off samples first — small lab-dip samples used purely for colour approval — before committing to a full lab sample. Once colour is approved, request lab samples (typically 1-3 metres of the actual construction) for hand feel and quality approval. Approving colour and construction as two separate steps, rather than in one pass, catches problems earlier and cheaper than discovering a hand-feel issue after a full development sample has already been produced.",
